      "textEn": "37\n\nDorbhyam—with one's arms; Parishvajya—by embracing; Rama—of Lakshmi; Amal—pure; Alayam—of the house; Mukunda—of Lord Krishna; Gatram—of the body; Nri-patih—King; Hata—destroyed; Ashubha—inauspicious; Lebhe—obtained; Param—highest;\nNirvrutti—joy; Ashru—tears; Lochanah—in whose eyes; Hrishyat—became pleased; Tanu—body; Vismrutah—forgotten; Lokah—of the world; Vibhramah—illusory activities..\nThe eternal form of Lord Krishna is the eternal abode of Lakshmi. As soon as Yudhishthira embraced him, he was freed from all material impurities. They immediately experienced divine bliss,\nand they were immersed in the ocean of happiness. Tears came into their eyes, and from being overwhelmed with emotion,\ntheir body began to tremble. He completely forgot that he is living in this material world. Meaning: The above meaning is from Srila Prabhupada, Lord Krishna. That mother, being free from the burden of others,\nBhima, with a mind filled with love and watery eyes.\nYamo Kiriti cha suhruttamam muda\nPravriddhabashpah parirebhiyu achyutam. 27. Meaning of the word\n\nTam—to him; Matuleyam—to the son of Mama; Parirabhya—by embracing; Nirvritah—filled with joy; Bhimah—Bhimasena; Smayan—\nlaughing; Prem—in love; Jal—from water; Akul—filled; Indriya—eyes; Yamau—twins (Nakula and Sahadeva);\nKiriti—Arjuna; Cha—and; Suhrut-Tamam—their dearest friend; Muda—with joy; Pravriddha—extremely; Bashpah—tears;\nParirebhire—by embracing; Achyutam—to Achyuta Bhagavan. Then, with tears in his eyes, Bhima embraced his cousin brother Krishna and then laughed with joy. Arjun and the twin brothers—Nakul and Sahadev—also embraced their most beloved friend,\nAchyut Bhagwan, with joy and started crying loudly. Arjuna was refuted by them and was rebuked. Salutations to the Brahmins and elders, as appropriate.\nManino manayamas kurusrijnjayakayanan. 28 ”. Meaning of the word\n\nArjunena—by Arjuna; Parishvaktaḥ—embraced; Yamabhyām—by the twins; Abhivaditah—welcomed; Brahmānebhyāḥ—to 