      "textEn": "1\n\nUchu-kha; Stri-ha; Pathi-ha; Nirikshya-ha; Mukunda-ha; Patni-ha;\nTara-ha; Yatha-ha; Udu-pa-ha; Chandra-ha; Saha-ha; Kim-ha; Aakari-ha; Amubhi-ha;\nBy them; Yat-ha; Because; Chakshusha-ha; For their eyes; Purusha-ha; Mauli-ha; Choti-ha; Kalaya-ha; Laghu-sa; Lila-ha; Aaloka-ha; Kalpanika-ha; Kalaya-ha; Kalaya-ha; Kalaya-ha; Kalaya-ha; Kalaya-ha; Kalaya-ha; Kalaya-ha; Kalaya-ha; Kalaya-ha; Kalaya-ha; Kalaya-ha; Kalaya-ha; Kalaya-ha; Kalaya-ha; Kalaya-ha; Kalaya- On the path, seeing Mukunda's wives passing by like stars with the moon, the women\n\nshouted, \"What deed have these women done, that the best person is giving pleasure to their eyes with his generous smile and playful long gazes?\"”\n\nThere, there, gathering, the auspicious hands.\nChakrulu Saparyam Krishnaya Shrenimukhya Hatainasah. 36. Meaning of the word\n\nThere—in various places; Upasangamya—to arrive; Paurah—citizens; Mangal—auspicious offerings; Panayah—in one's own hands; Chakrur—\ncompleted; Saparyam—worship; Krishnaya—for Krishna; Shreni—of the merchants; Mukhyah—chief leader; Hata—destroyed;\nEnasah—sin I.\n\nIn various places, the citizens of the city brought auspicious offerings for Krishna, and the chief\ninnocent merchants proceeded to worship the Lord. Meaning: Srila Prabhupada writes, \"When Lord Krishna was going on the path, some wealthy,\nprestigious, and innocent citizens of the city, to welcome him at the city's entrance, offered Lord Krishna auspicious\nobjects. In this way, they worshipped him as a humble servant.\"\n\nBy the inner chamber's people, with love, Mukunda, with full eyes.\nSasambhramairabhyupetah: Pravishadrajamandiram. 37. Meaning of the word\n\n[^1]: Antah-pur—of the inner apartments; Janaih—by the people; Pritiya—lovingly; Mukundah—Lord Krishna; Phulla—jasmine; Lochanaih—with eyes; Sa-sambhramaih—in enthusiasm; Abhyupetah—welcomed; Pravishat—entered; Raja—royal; Mandiram—palace\nin. With tearful eyes, the members of the inner palace lovingly welcomed Lord Mukunda with enthusiasm,\nand thus, the Lord entered the palace. [^2]: Seeing the brother, Krishna, the lord of the three worlds. Pritatmatthaya parinkatassnusha parishasvaje. 38. Lexicon"
